meta {
  name: Ws
  type: ws
  seq: 2
}

ws {
  url: {{coreApiUrl}}/api/v1/ws?token={{accessToken}}
  body: ws
  auth: inherit
}

body:ws {
  name: message 1
  type: json
  content: '''
  
  '''
}

docs {
  Bruno sends this as a plain GET, so expect a 426 or 400 from the upgrader. It is here to document the endpoint. Connect with a real client instead:
  
  ```bash
  websocat "ws://localhost:8080/api/v1/ws?token=$ACCESS_TOKEN"
  ```
  
  or in a browser:
  
  ```js
  const ws = new WebSocket(`ws://localhost:8080/api/v1/ws?token=${token}`);
  ws.onmessage = (e) => console.log(JSON.parse(e.data));
  ```
  
  Auth: `token` query param or `Authorization: Bearer` header (any role).
  
  Frames from the server:
  
  ```json
  { "type": "hello", "user_id": "uuid", "at": "..." }
  { "type": "event", "subject": "incident.created", "payload": { "type": "...", "occurred_at": "...", "source": "core-api", "data": { } } }
  ```
  
  The server pings every 30 s and drops clients that fall more than 64 frames behind.
}
